So she's been on my show.

00:16:07.399 --> 00:16:08.834
I think she's wonderful.

00:16:08.834 --> 00:16:10.569 align:start size:97% position:3%
Obviously we have some
disagreements on this stuff.

00:16:10.569 --> 00:16:12.571
I have put out there
many times on Twitter

00:16:12.571 --> 00:16:15.240
I would love to have
a pro-choice advocate

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.875
come on the show with Lila Rose.

00:16:16.875 --> 00:16:19.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've invited Alyssa
Milano and the collection

00:16:19.745 --> 00:16:22.381
of usual suspects,
totally respectfully,

00:16:22.381 --> 00:16:26.185 align:start size:97% position:3%
we've reached out publicly
and privately, nobody, nobody,

00:16:26.185 --> 00:16:27.453
and there's a reason for it.

00:16:27.453 --> 00:16:29.655 line:0%
It's not just that
Dave Rubin is mean

00:16:29.655 --> 00:16:32.458 line:0%
or something like that
or that Lila's a liar

00:16:32.458 --> 00:16:33.659 line:0%
or something like that.

00:16:33.659 --> 00:16:35.194 line:0%
These are not true
statements obviously.

00:16:35.194 --> 00:16:38.497
It's that they don't want to
actually debate these things

00:16:38.497 --> 00:16:41.100
in a calm way because
they need the emotion

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.434
to override the argument.

00:16:42.434 --> 00:16:43.969
So how do you beat the mob?

00:16:43.969 --> 00:16:46.338 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, the mob actually
preys on the fact

00:16:46.338 --> 00:16:48.073
that people are afraid.

00:16:48.073 --> 00:16:49.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think there's a
lot of people that think,

00:16:49.575 --> 00:16:51.610
oh, if I could just beat,
I can sit this one out.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.112
Let me just sit this one out,

00:16:53.112 --> 00:16:55.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
let me be quiet this time,
it'll pass, it'll pass.

00:16:55.447 --> 00:16:56.348
It doesn't pass.

00:16:56.348 --> 00:16:57.282
That's the thing.

00:16:57.282 --> 00:16:58.650
They have preyed on the fact

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:01.687
that good people are good people

00:17:01.687 --> 00:17:03.655
and they have used
that against us.

00:17:03.655 --> 00:17:06.325
And it's the frog
in the boiling pot.

00:17:06.325 --> 00:17:08.627
If you think that
your acquiescence

00:17:08.627 --> 00:17:11.063 align:start size:84% position:16%
or that your silence
is saving you,

00:17:11.063 --> 00:17:13.632
you're actually turning
the dial up on the pot

00:17:13.632 --> 00:17:15.134
that you are in.

00:17:15.134 --> 00:17:17.636
And as you know, it does not
end well for the frog, right?

00:17:17.636 --> 00:17:19.838
Like that frog is fried
at the end of that thing.

00:17:19.838 --> 00:17:22.041
And I think that that is
what has happened here.

00:17:22.041 --> 00:17:24.009
And that in many ways is why
I wanted to write the book

00:17:24.009 --> 00:17:25.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
more than anything else
because that was the idea.

00:17:25.778 --> 00:17:29.448 align:start size:97% position:3%
It was like I don't think
that everything I present here

00:17:29.448 --> 00:17:33.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the most legendary,
political idea of all time

00:17:33.285 --> 00:17:35.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I think I've been
able to communicate ideas

00:17:35.287 --> 00:17:38.624
in a good way and I've
paid the price for that.

00:17:39.792 --> 00:17:42.194 align:start size:88% position:13%
- And there are rewards-
- Absolutely.

00:17:42.194 --> 00:17:43.662 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Based on the
price you paid too.

00:17:43.662 --> 00:17:45.998
- And I don't say paid the
price to get any pity points.

00:17:45.998 --> 00:17:47.399
I don't want any pity points.

00:17:47.399 --> 00:17:48.767
I've gotten the rewards
of that took, right?

00:17:48.767 --> 00:17:51.303
It's awesome, it's cool.

00:17:51.303 --> 00:17:53.205 align:start size:84% position:16%
I wake up and I'm
ready to go every day.

00:17:53.205 --> 00:17:56.408 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
- How do you feel like we
can emotionally arm ourselves

00:17:56.408 --> 00:17:59.178 line:0%
for taking on backlash?

00:17:59.178 --> 00:18:01.613 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because if we want to be great
in our lives at any stage,

00:18:01.613 --> 00:18:04.650
any a decade of our life,

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:07.219 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's going to be critics,
haters, backlash, mob,

00:18:07.219 --> 00:18:09.888
whether it's online,
offline, whatever.

00:18:09.888 --> 00:18:12.191 align:start position:0%
What do you think we can do
emotionally to prepare for that?

00:18:12.191 --> 00:18:14.093 align:start size:84% position:16%
Besides what I think
is the best thing

00:18:14.093 --> 00:18:17.229
is just to do it as
often as possible

00:18:17.229 --> 00:18:19.631
to be able to stomach it and
say, okay, I'm still alive.

00:18:19.631 --> 00:18:21.967 align:start size:81% position:19%
I'm still here.
It didn't kill me.

00:18:21.967 --> 00:18:24.236
It hurts, but I'm stronger.

00:18:24.236 --> 00:18:25.838 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well, partly it's
that, partly it's that.

00:18:25.838 --> 00:18:27.339
Partly it's basketball
has been a theme here.

00:18:27.339 --> 00:18:30.075 align:start size:97% position:3%
So like partly it's why did
Michael Jordan practice harder

00:18:30.075 --> 00:18:31.276
than anybody else?

00:18:31.276 --> 00:18:32.311
Right? Like that
is the known thing.

00:18:32.311 --> 00:18:33.712
Kobe was like it too.

00:18:33.712 --> 00:18:35.013
It's like why did they do it?

00:18:35.013 --> 00:18:36.715
Barkley didn't love practice,

00:18:36.715 --> 00:18:39.818
Allen Iverson famously,
"Practice!", you know?

00:18:39.818 --> 00:18:41.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's not to say
they weren't great players

00:18:41.887 --> 00:18:43.522
but Allen Iverson
and Charles Barkley

00:18:43.522 --> 00:18:44.723
never won championships.

00:18:44.723 --> 00:18:46.792
And Michael Jordan
won six championships

00:18:46.792 --> 00:18:48.293 align:start size:88% position:13%
and he was in the
final six times, right?

00:18:48.293 --> 00:18:50.395
And he's systematically
eliminated every one

00:18:50.395 --> 00:18:51.763
of his peers to get there.

00:18:51.763 --> 00:18:55.200 align:start size:88% position:13%
So partly it's just that
you got to, you know,

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:56.668
Douglas Murray who
I've had on my show,

00:18:56.668 --> 00:18:58.971 align:start size:97% position:3%
who is a brilliant
Conservative political thinker

00:18:58.971 --> 00:19:00.806
from the UK and one of
the greatest writers

00:19:00.806 --> 00:19:03.008 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I think we have
in modern times.

00:19:03.008 --> 00:19:04.977
He said to me once, he said,

00:19:04.977 --> 00:19:08.680 align:start size:97% position:3%
"If you get in the pool,"
he said in a British accent.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:11.450
"If you dip your toe in the pool

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:14.386
you might find out that the
water is not that cold."

00:19:14.386 --> 00:19:16.555
And I actually think that
that's the right idea.

00:19:16.555 --> 00:19:18.957 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's nothing to
fear, but fear itself.

00:19:18.957 --> 00:19:22.628 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's something like that,
that we create these monsters.

00:19:22.628 --> 00:19:24.563
And then when you
actually go ahead

00:19:24.563 --> 00:19:26.498 align:start size:84% position:16%
and do whatever
you're supposed to do,

00:19:26.498 --> 00:19:28.467 align:start size:84% position:16%
you might step in
the pool and be like

00:19:28.467 --> 00:19:30.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
damn, I thought the water
was gonna be freezing

00:19:30.135 --> 00:19:31.737
but it turns out it's 92.

00:19:31.737 --> 00:19:32.971 align:start size:84% position:16%
- [Lewis] It's fresh,
yeah, it's fresh.

00:19:32.971 --> 00:19:33.906
- And that's not to say
it's gonna be perfect

00:19:33.906 --> 00:19:34.706
'cause trust me, it won't be.

00:19:34.706 --> 00:19:36.175
You will lose friends.

00:19:36.175 --> 00:19:37.543
I mean, we've all been
through versions of this.

00:19:37.543 --> 00:19:39.344 align:start size:84% position:16%
People that you love
will suddenly say

00:19:39.344 --> 00:19:40.512
the worst things about you.

00:19:40.512 --> 00:19:42.381
I'm seeing some of this now.

00:19:42.381 --> 00:19:45.184
I'm getting a lot of support

00:19:45.184 --> 00:19:47.319 align:start size:84% position:16%
from my sort of
right-leaning friends.

00:19:47.319 --> 00:19:49.922
So you know, Shapiro and
Peterson and Glenn Beck

00:19:49.922 --> 00:19:51.156
and Dennis Prager, that crew.

00:19:51.156 --> 00:19:53.325
A lot of my lefty guys
who had been with me

00:19:53.325 --> 00:19:55.160
all along the road have
completely abandoned me

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.862
because they don't
want to just deal

00:19:56.862 --> 00:19:58.130
with any of the backlash.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:19:59.798
And I also think this
is a whole other topic

00:19:59.798 --> 00:20:02.234
but I think that goes to a
little bit of the lefty mind

00:20:02.234 --> 00:20:04.303 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is in constant
protection mode.

00:20:04.303 --> 00:20:06.738
That's like sort of like
a whole separate thing

00:20:06.738 --> 00:20:10.342
but you gotta get
in, get in the game

00:20:10.342 --> 00:20:12.544 align:start size:84% position:16%
because the game is
coming for you anyway,

00:20:12.544 --> 00:20:15.147
whether you, you can
say I'm not playing,

00:20:15.147 --> 00:20:16.615 align:start size:88% position:13%
but it's what we talked
about with politics

00:20:16.615 --> 00:20:18.784
before the game is
being played, man.

00:20:18.784 --> 00:20:20.052
That's like saying, you know,

00:20:20.052 --> 00:20:21.320
if we were looking
at a chess board,

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:22.788
it's like you are
one of the pieces

00:20:22.788 --> 00:20:24.022
whether you like it or not.

00:20:24.022 --> 00:20:26.558
And if the whole board
is being shifted around,

00:20:26.558 --> 00:20:28.493
well, you got to move with it.

00:20:28.493 --> 00:20:30.629
- They will have a journalist on

00:20:30.629 --> 00:20:32.864 line:0%
and he'll say the equivalent

00:20:34.633 --> 00:20:37.102 line:0%
of two towers, 9/11.

00:20:37.102 --> 00:20:38.403 align:start size:84% position:16%
People died.
- These are horrible

00:20:38.403 --> 00:20:39.371
equivalence comparisons.
- The equivalent of that

00:20:39.371 --> 00:20:40.439
is dying every single day

00:20:40.439 --> 00:20:41.807
and people still don't get it.

00:20:41.807 --> 00:20:44.042 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it's like, is that
what you're saying?

00:20:44.042 --> 00:20:47.879
And do you mind like having
some caveats around that?

00:20:47.879 --> 00:20:49.281
How old are they?

00:20:49.281 --> 00:20:51.049
Are we sure of that?

00:20:51.049 --> 00:20:52.517
Are they all being tested?

00:20:52.517 --> 00:20:55.020 align:start size:97% position:3%
There are all of these
questions where you're like,

00:20:56.421 --> 00:20:59.057 align:start position:0%
it's almost like they want
this lockdown to go on forever.

00:20:59.057 --> 00:21:00.692
- They do, well, first
off their ratings are up

00:21:00.692 --> 00:21:02.427
in the midst of this because
we're all trapped at home.

00:21:02.427 --> 00:21:03.962
So let's not, the media is dead.

00:21:03.962 --> 00:21:05.831 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, that's an
important thing to just,

00:21:05.831 --> 00:21:07.466 align:start size:84% position:16%
we have to just
say it and know it.

00:21:07.466 --> 00:21:09.701
The mainstream media
is just absolute dead.

00:21:09.701 --> 00:21:11.737 align:start size:75% position:25%
CNN is the WWE.
- It is.

00:21:11.737 --> 00:21:14.072 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I mean, I think that moment
when you saw that moment

00:21:14.072 --> 00:21:16.375 align:start size:97% position:3%
when Chris Cuomo walked out
of his basement and they said,

00:21:16.375 --> 00:21:18.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, he's been in
quarantine for three weeks

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:20.178
and here he comes."

00:21:20.178 --> 00:21:21.179
And he had the shivers
and he chipped a tooth

00:21:21.179 --> 00:21:22.447
because he had COVID and blah.

00:21:22.447 --> 00:21:23.982
And it's like he comes
up and he's sweating.

00:21:23.982 --> 00:21:25.917
And then he announces, oh, it
was 'cause he was working out

00:21:25.917 --> 00:21:27.019
downstairs while he had COVID.

00:21:27.019 --> 00:21:29.254
The whole thing, it's all fixed.

00:21:29.254 --> 00:21:30.856
I mean, just a week
before he had said

00:21:30.856 --> 00:21:32.424 align:start size:84% position:16%
he was in quarantine
for three weeks,

00:21:32.424 --> 00:21:34.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
it turns out a week
before he got into a fight

00:21:34.726 --> 00:21:36.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a biker outside of
his house in the Hamptons.

00:21:36.928 --> 00:21:39.831
- Correct and there's video.
- It's all made up nonsense.

00:21:39.831 --> 00:21:42.367
We are watching WWE skits

00:21:42.367 --> 00:21:44.136
in front of us and
pretending it's real.

00:21:44.136 --> 00:21:45.971
- But why don't people get it?

00:21:45.971 --> 00:21:48.206 align:start size:81% position:19%
- So I'm on a book
tour right now.

00:21:48.206 --> 00:21:50.842
I have done every freaking
podcast you can think of.

00:21:50.842 --> 00:21:53.211
I've been on every
Fox show repeatedly.

00:21:53.211 --> 00:21:55.013
I would go on every
single CNN show,

00:21:55.013 --> 00:21:56.515
here I'm saying it again.

00:21:56.515 --> 00:21:59.284
I have not gotten one invite,
not one invite from MSNBC.

00:21:59.284 --> 00:22:00.319
- They're just afraid of you.

00:22:00.319 --> 00:22:02.487
- My only caveat
though would be,

00:22:02.487 --> 00:22:03.955
I would only do it live

00:22:03.955 --> 00:22:05.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I don't trust
them on the editing side.

00:22:05.357 --> 00:22:06.625
But Fox, I go on live.

00:22:06.625 --> 00:22:08.060
They don't tell me
to say anything.

00:22:08.060 --> 00:22:10.362 align:start size:97% position:3%
I was supposed to be on
Perino right before I got here

00:22:10.362 --> 00:22:11.897 align:start size:84% position:16%
but then this
Flynn story dropped

00:22:11.897 --> 00:22:13.365
so they canceled me
at the last second.

00:22:13.365 --> 00:22:14.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
- We are so polarized,
aren't we in this country,

00:22:14.666 --> 00:22:15.934
I mean, it's just so fucking-

00:22:15.934 --> 00:22:17.869
- Well, I think most
of us are like this.

00:22:19.237 --> 00:22:21.039 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
- I think we're the
fortunate ones, don't you?

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:23.408 line:0%
- We're fortunate in that

00:22:23.408 --> 00:22:26.311 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
we're not like completely
partisan crazy people

00:22:26.311 --> 00:22:28.780 align:start size:97% position:3%
wandering around thinking
that Nazis are hunting us down

00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:31.550
or that half the country is
evil or something like that.

00:22:31.550 --> 00:22:32.818
Most people aren't.

00:22:32.818 --> 00:22:35.120 line:0%
- There's really a
lot of ways to win

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:37.823 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
this presidential
election for Democrats

00:22:37.823 --> 00:22:40.492 line:0%
and it's not just getting
all those crusty white guys

00:22:40.492 --> 00:22:43.462 line:0%
in diners in the Midwest.

00:22:43.462 --> 00:22:45.831 line:0%
Nothing against guys and
diners in the Midwest.

00:22:48.967 --> 00:22:51.403 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
- I swear the Trump campaign
is paying that a woman.

00:22:51.403 --> 00:22:52.904 line:0%
She's just an ad for Trump.

00:22:52.904 --> 00:22:55.407 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
Dave Rubin joins us from
The Rubin Report on YouTube.

00:22:55.407 --> 00:22:57.175 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Our old friend joins
us here on set.

00:22:57.175 --> 00:22:58.343 line:0%
Dave, great to see you tonight.

00:22:58.343 --> 00:22:59.311 line:0%
- It's good to see you.

00:22:59.311 --> 00:23:00.245 line:0%
Before you say anything, Tucker,

00:23:00.245 --> 00:23:01.413 line:0%
I just want to be very clear.

00:23:01.413 --> 00:23:02.280 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
The woman you're talking
about right there.

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:03.081 align:start size:72% position:28% line:0%
In that clip.
- Yes.

00:23:03.081 --> 00:23:03.882 line:0%
- That's Jennifer Rubin.

00:23:03.882 --> 00:23:05.117 line:0%
I am in no way related.

00:23:05.117 --> 00:23:06.118 line:0%
- I totally forgot you
had the same last name.

00:23:06.118 --> 00:23:07.386 line:0%
- Very important
that I say that.

00:23:07.386 --> 00:23:09.554 line:0%
- Well, she's a plant,
clearly she's a plant.

00:23:09.554 --> 00:23:11.089 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- What kind of
Conservative is she?

00:23:11.089 --> 00:23:13.592 line:0%
- She and Jeb Bush's former
spokeswoman who's on MSNBC,

00:23:13.592 --> 00:23:15.026 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
you watch them and you're
like, you know what?

00:23:15.026 --> 00:23:16.228 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
I'm voting for
Trump. I don't care.

00:23:16.228 --> 00:23:18.330 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
- It's really confusing.
- It's unbelievable.

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:20.098 line:0%
Anyway, let me ask you

00:23:21.266 --> 00:23:23.869 line:0%
how dehumanizing
do you think it is

00:23:23.869 --> 00:23:26.271 line:0%
to see people in the
media who appear intent

00:23:26.271 --> 00:23:28.039 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
on dividing the country
along racial lines

00:23:28.039 --> 00:23:29.875 line:0%
to dismiss people on the
basis of their skin color?

00:23:29.875 --> 00:23:31.410 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
Like how do we
get to this place?

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:34.379 line:0%
- Who was that guy that wanted
his children not to be judged

00:23:34.379 --> 00:23:35.547 line:0%
by the color of their skin?

00:23:35.547 --> 00:23:36.915 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- There's a monument
to him, yeah.

00:23:36.915 --> 00:23:38.316 line:0%
- The content of
their character.

00:23:38.316 --> 00:23:39.818 line:0%
That guy was kind of right.

00:23:39.818 --> 00:23:41.753 line:0%
That guy, MLK Jr. Obviously,

00:23:41.753 --> 00:23:44.189 line:0%
he was a liberal,
he was a liberal

00:23:44.189 --> 00:23:46.425 line:0%
but the progressives
have nothing to do

00:23:46.425 --> 00:23:47.559 line:0%
with true liberalism.

00:23:47.559 --> 00:23:49.227 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
And there's a
hilarity going on here

00:23:49.227 --> 00:23:52.898 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
because for years they've
been screaming that all of us,

00:23:52.898 --> 00:23:55.467 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
anyone who's not a woke
intersectional progressive

00:23:55.467 --> 00:23:56.968 line:0%
is a racist.

00:23:56.968 --> 00:23:58.870 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
But what was gonna be at
the end of the road of that?

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:00.806 line:0%
At the end of the
road is exactly

